    "Fine Woodworking video selection: a READING pass, 2026-09-07.",
    "",
    "243 candidates from scripts/youtube_channel.py over 23 period-furniture",
    "terms. ⚠ The hit counts are page size, not relevance -- see that script.",
    "",
    "⚠ SHOP TALK LIVE IS EXCLUDED WHOLESALE. Roughly 90 of the 243 candidates are",
    "STL podcast episodes, and their titles are jokes ('Dinkle dreams of bed",
    "frames', 'The facebook bark police'). A handful genuinely name a subject and",
    "an authority -- 'STL 88: Marquetry Master Craig Thibodeau' really is about",
    "marquetry -- but they are hour-long chat shows, and a card promising research",
    "that delivers a podcast is worse than no card. This is the P&T punning-",
    "headline lesson arriving from the other direction: there, titles hid real",
    "articles; here, they advertise substance a listener will spend an hour not",
    "finding. If STL is ever wanted, it is a separate decision with its own",
    "treatment, not a keyword sweep.",
    "",
    "⚠ ALSO EXCLUDED, deliberately: machine/jig/tool-maintenance content (bandsaw",
    "drift, router bits, jointer shimming), Domino/biscuit/pocket-hole joinery,",
    "greenwood bowl and spoon carving, kumiko and Chinese joinery. All good",
    "woodworking; none of it is American period furniture, which is the tent this",
    "catalog serves.",
    "",
    "⚠ THE STANDING COMMITMENT. Unlike the Met, whose furniture holdings are",
    "bounded and evergreen, Fine Woodworking publishes constantly. This file is a",
    "snapshot of a back catalog; keeping it current is an ongoing curation job,",
    "not a one-off. Re-run the sweep and read the new titles -- do not automate it.",
    "",
    "Tag vocabularies are the ones already in library_cards. The Met set skews to",
    "objects and connoisseurship; this one skews to Construction / Technique,",
    "because the two publishers do different jobs -- the same split the P&T/APF",
    "subject map found between our own two publications."
